        "title": "Finishing: Oils, Shellac, Lacquer, Varnish, Water-Based",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Wood finish serves two functions: protection (from moisture, scratches, staining) and appearance (color, sheen, depth). The chemistry of the finish determines how it cures, how it builds, how to repair it, and whether it's compatible with other finishes. Getting the chemistry wrong — applying incompatible products — can prevent curing or cause permanent adhesion failure."
    },
