        "section": "woodworking",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Finishing: Oils, Shellac, Lacquer, Varnish, Water-Based",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "BOILED LINSEED OIL (BLO):\n  Chemistry: linseed oil + metallic driers (cobalt, manganese)\n             cures by oxidative polymerization\n  Drying: 24–72 hours per coat (true linseed: months; BLO: days)\n  Coats needed: 3–5 for any protection\n  Result: low sheen; yellow-amber; \"Danish\" look\n  Protection: poor; penetrates but provides little barrier\n  Problems: spontaneous combustion risk (rags soaked in oil must be\n            spread flat to dry or submerged in water in sealed container)\n  Best for: tool handles, carving, shop items (not furniture)"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-FINISHING.md#013",
      "path": [
        "06-FINISHING.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
