        "title": "Finishing: Oils, Shellac, Lacquer, Varnish, Water-Based",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "TUNG OIL (pure):\n  Chemistry: Tung nut oil; cures by oxidation + polymerization\n             more water-resistant than BLO when cured\n  Drying: 24–48 hours per coat\n  Result: very low sheen (matte); does not darken as much as BLO\n  Coats: 3–5\n  Important: most products labeled \"tung oil\" are NOT pure tung oil\n             (they're wiping varnish — see below)"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-FINISHING.md#015",
      "path": [
        "06-FINISHING.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:woodworking:06-finishing, git-history:woodworking:06-finishing]",
